WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.500
Привет, Датминс Хэллоин Рашен.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:09.560
Welcome to привет, русский, Episode 43, its 18 июня 2026 года.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.360
I'm Olya, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:14.980
Ready?

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.080
Поехали, Датминс, let's go.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.240
Our word of the day is хлеб.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:22.400
хлеб.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.000
It sounds a little like loaf, and both are the staff of life.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.260
Repeat after me, хлеб.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.880
Now listen to it in a sentence.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.960
Я ем хлеб, that means I eat bread.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.500
Let's build our food vocabulary.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.760
Our first new word is яблоко.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.220
It sounds like apple with a friendly co-ending.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.120
Repeat after me, яблоко, яблоко.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.640
This is a big apple, it's a big apple.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.440
Next comes молоко, молоко, мол.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.480
The last syllable pops like milk, splatement to our glass.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:09.020
Repeat after me, молоко, молоко, I drink milk, я пью молоко.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.060
Now we have сыр, сыр, it's short and cheesy.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.280
Just like the English word serve, but it means cheese.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.280
Repeat after me, сыр, сыр.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.640
The cheese is delicious, сыр вкусный.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.260
Our next word is мясо, и мясо, а Джейзу.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.500
Imagine a meaty lion saying my A.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.440
Repeat after me, my A, my A, the meat is big, мясо большое.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:39.360
Here is овощ, овощ.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.720
It sounds like off-fresh, perfect for garden vegetables.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:48.100
Repeat after me, овощ, овощ.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:51.920
The vegetable is delicious, овощ вкусный.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.900
Next is fruct, fruct.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.240
It is almost the same as the English word fruct and easy win.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.360
Repeat after me, fruct, fruct.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.160
An apple is a fruit, я облако это fruct.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.980
Now we'll learn to action words, есть, means to eat, есть.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:14.620
It sounds like, есть, so say, yes to eating.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.100
Repeat after me, есть, есть.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.680
I eat bread, я есть хлеб.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:25.840
Пить, means to drink, it rhymes with it, but means drink.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.660
Repeat after me, пить, пить, I drink milk, я пить молоко.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.980
Remember my from earlier lessons, my it is your personal word.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:44.360
My apple, my apple, remember большое ту, боль, боль, шои.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.700
Think of a big show of food on your plate, beat cheese, большой сыр.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:51.980
Now fork with grammar bite.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.660
Every Russian noun has a gender, masculine, feminine or neuter.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:06.080
Хлеб, ens in a consonant, so it is masculine, я облака, ens in o, so it is neuter, молоко is also neuter.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:13.540
Adjective a must match the noun like, большое яблоко, for a big apple, but, большое сыр, for big cheese.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.360
The words hold hands, Russian love sharing food, especially bread and tea.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.680
When guests arrive, host always over chat with something sweet.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:29.600
Before eating, people say, приятного аппетита, to show they care about everyone at the table.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.660
For our practice challenge, draw your favorite food and label it with today's Russian words.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.040
Then say, я им, followed by the food name out loud.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.080
Adults name three items on your plate in Russian, the next time you eat.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.020
Want to know a secret about one of the days' words?

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:55.660
Did you know the Russian word, чай, and the English word, т, are actually cousins from the same ancient route?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:03.080
The word started in чайна, as чай, traveled along the Silk Road through Persian and Turkey's traders,

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.980
and reached Russian in the 17th century.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:12.140
Be careful, though, the Russian word, магазин, sounds like magazine, but actually means shop.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:17.940
Next time you see, tea, remember it shares the same Chinese route with чай и чай.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:20.960
That connection is your secret shortcut.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.280
And that's our lesson for today.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:25.320
Молодец, fast-taking, but it.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:30.140
Try using today's words in one real sentence before the next episode.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.160
Little steps, big progress.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.100
Пока, friends.

